From 6e6fdb753dca378137a60dcbf14b9ddd2df3ea5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:43:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] fix(router): decode SGLang's bigram BlockStored tokens
 under MTP

From PR #56 (liyingli), reduced to the Python router this merge exercised.

With EAGLE/MTP on, SGLang keys its radix tree on bigrams (RadixKey.is_bigram,
set from is_eagle) and the kv-event emitter reports a block's tokens as the
overlapping pairs (t[i], t[i+1]). The client hashed the pairs as-is while the
query side chunks the flat token slice, so the view could never be matched:
cache_hits pinned at 0 and kv-aware routing degrading to round-robin, silently,
because nothing in the pipeline errors.

Take the first element of each pair -- that rebuilds t[start:end], the slice
hash_request chunks, and radix nodes split on page boundaries so the two
chunkings stay aligned. Widen the msgspec schema to the union it really is, or
every event fails to decode before reaching the hasher.

Note is_eagle is a GLOBAL server arg, so this bites the PREFILL leg too, not
only the leg running MTP. That is what makes it observable in a PD run whose
decode leg alone has MTP on.

Deliberately NOT taken from PR#56's 01b0534:

  * rust/router/src/kv_event.rs and its tests -- the same bug in the Rust
    decoder. Every run in this merge used --router-backend python (the
    default), so we never exercised that path. PR #56 carries the fix; until
    it lands, a Rust-router deployment with MTP still has the original bug.

Validated here by G1: the router's mirrored KV view reads 51 blocks on the
prefill worker, byte-identical to the plain-int path in G0. Unfixed it reads 0.

Co-authored-by: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
